<problem>
<!-- <title>Derivative of logarithm times polynomial with quadratic and cubic terms</title>
 -->
<setup>

<selectFromSequence name="a" numToSelect="2" from="-10" to=" 10" exclude="0" />
<!-- Original required condition was Or($a ,$b ) -->

<select name="function"> u v w x y z</select>
<select name="x"> s t</select>

<math name="cubic" simplify="full">$a[1] *$x ^3+$a[2] *$x ^2</math>
<math name="d_cubic" simplify="full">3*$a[1] *$x ^2+2*$a[2] *$x </math>
<math name="d_f" simplify="full">$d_cubic *ln($x )+$a[1] *$x ^2+$a[2] *$x </math>

</setup>


Calculate the derivative of <m>$function ($x ) = ($cubic  ) \ln ($x )</m>.

<p><m>$function'($x) = </m>
<answer forceFullCheckworkButton="true"><award>$d_f</award></answer>
</p>

<hint>
<p>You'll need to use the product rule</p>

<paragraphs>
<title>Helpful pages</title>
<ul>
<li><ref to="doenet:7Lv5ho8yHm7pNZA3UeSyG2">The idea of the product rule</ref></li>
</ul></paragraphs>
</hint>


<solution>
<p>By the <ref to="doenet:7Lv5ho8yHm7pNZA3UeSyG2">product rule</ref>



<md>
  <mrow>$function '($x )\amp =  ($cubic ) '\ln($x ) + ($cubic )  (\ln($x ))'</mrow>
  <mrow>\amp = ($d_cubic )  \ln($x ) +  ($cubic )  \frac{1}{ $x  }</mrow>
  <mrow>\amp = $d_f  .</mrow>
</md>
</p>


</solution>


</problem>